<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47520" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἡρακλεώτης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a man of Heraclea</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1327b14
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1271
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ειώτης</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				12.145
			</span></i>):—Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἡρακλεωτικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <i>of
				Heraclea</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				525b5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅμμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Heracl.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				48.8.1
			</span></i>; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρύα</span>] <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				1.10.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.6.5
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Zopyr.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				14.50.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμύγδαλα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Diocl.Fr.
					126
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρίγανος -κή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philum.
					<u>Ven.</u>
					16.9
				</span></i>
			; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκύφος Ἡρακλεωτικός</span>
			is said to derive its name directly from <u>Heracles</u>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				11.500a
			</span></i>:—fem. also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἡρακλειτ-ῶτις</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				3.3.8
			</span></i>, al.</div>
